WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.573
RetoMaton stores each datastore entry as a triple
of key, value, and pointer,

00:00:04.653 --> 00:00:08.803
where the pointer references the entry that
followed it in the corpus.

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:11.824
Entries with close keys are clustered into states,

00:00:11.904 --> 00:00:15.026
and a state inherits all the pointers of its members.

00:00:15.106 --> 00:00:21.975
At test time the model keeps a small set of active
states and traverses the automaton alongside the language model.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:27.776
To move forward it just follows the pointers of
entries whose value matches the generated token,

00:00:27.856 --> 00:00:29.347
which is essentially free.

00:00:29.427 --> 00:00:34.906
A full nearest-neighbor search is only triggered
when the number of valid onward transitions

00:00:34.986 --> 00:00:36.598
drops below a threshold tau.

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:41.734
The automaton's transition weights are computed
dynamically from the distance between

00:00:41.814 --> 00:00:45.058
the current hidden state and the entries in each state,

00:00:45.138 --> 00:00:49.650
and the resulting distribution is interpolated with
the base language model.
